      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson places B021 first, emphasizing that GLP-1 physiology joins an enduring endocrine mechanism to major therapeutic transformation in diabetes and obesity, while noting distributed drug-development credit.",
        "response": "I agree that B021 is an extraordinary and mature physiological and therapeutic advance, and retain it as the leading alternative. However, its proposed achievement spans hormone identification, physiology, receptor biology, pharmacology, and therapeutic development, leaving a more difficult boundary and allocation of credit than B002 on the supplied evidence."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann gives highest priority to B044 because distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages established a foundational organizing principle of adaptive immunity.",
        "response": "The scientific maturity and conceptual importance of B044 are unquestionable. I nevertheless favor B002 this round because it unites a comparably clear biological principle with demonstrated prevention of major cancers, whereas the supplied description of B044 leaves the broader experimental contribution and precise attribution beyond the two credited investigators less fully bounded."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the supplied three-person attribution for B002 adequately captures the respective foundational and translational contributions.",
      "Whether B021 can define a sufficiently bounded achievement and laureate allocation across GLP-1 biology and therapeutic development."
    ],
